cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ChronicleBench — the protocol, instrument, harness, or data — please cite it as below."
title: "ChronicleBench: an open, preregistered benchmark for sustained long-form generation"
authors:
  - name: "Chronicle (chronicle.town)"
type: dataset
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
url: "https://bench.chronicle.town"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mmaier88/chroniclebench"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - long-form generation
  - creative writing
  - preregistration
abstract: >-
  ChronicleBench measures whether an AI system can deliver a complete,
  commissioned 80-95,000-word novel and how good it is, scored on five
  positional 10,000-word windows against a 36-novel published public-domain
  reference corpus, under one frozen, preregistered protocol with a pinned
  evidence-cited rubric instrument. Data is CC BY 4.0; code is MIT.
